  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coverage by June Media of issues related to women and to LGBTQ+ people</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media June is the new (temporary) name of Media April which was compelled to open a new organisation because of the Law on Foreign Influence. It is the only (online) medium in Georgia that reports about issues related to LGBTQ+ people. During two months of this project, they will write about 100 articles, produce 50 video&apos;s and publish 200 online media products.

This contribution is meant to allow Media April / June to survive  at least after general elections of 2024 (November-December). Depending on the outcome of the elections, Media April will either continue fundraising (and they have preliminary confirmation from EED and other donors) or will close down its operations.

The recently adopted &quot;anti-LGBTI propaganda&quot; law (expected to come into force in about two months) will not ban Media June but they will have to put an &quot;18+&quot; barrier before accessing the website.</narrative>
  </description>
